<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">NOTES:  n  n1.The above financial results of the company have been reviewed  by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective meeting held on 29th day of June, 2020.  n  n2.The Company adopted Indian Accounting Standards ( Ind AS ) prescribed under section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 read with the relevant Rules issued thereunder from1st April, 2017.  n  n3.As a result of Covid-19 outbreak and nation-wide lockdown announced by the Government, operations of the company were temporarily suspended from 24.03.2020. On 03.04.2020, after obtaining necessary approval from Government authorities, the company has resumed its operation in a phased manner with adequate measures needed to restrict spread of Covid-19. Due to reduction in economic activities, it seems that demand of paper and paperboards would have a short-term decline, which is expected to recover in Q2 of 2020-21.  nThe company has made an assessment of possible impact of Covid-19 pandemic based on the current indicators of future economic conditions and measures taken by the Government; and does not anticipate any challenge in meeting its financial obligations and believes that it will be in a position to recover carrying amount of property plant &amp; equipment and other current / non-current assets. In the prevailing circumstances, the company does not expect any impact of Covid-19 on its ability to continue as a going concern.  n  n4.The company has adopted Ind AS 116  Leases  w.e.f. 01.04.2019; under the modified retrospective approach without adjustment of comparatives. Application of this standard does not have any material impact on the profitability for the quarter and year ended 31.03.2020.  n  n5.On 30.05.2019, equity shares of the company get listed on National Stock Exchange. It was already listed with Bombay Stock Exchange since 2010.  n  n6. Exceptional Item represents pre-operative expenses of Rs.27.00 crore incurred in FY 2018-19 for green field multi-layer paperboard expansion project in Bharuch, Gujarat, which was discontinued in September, 2019.  n  n7. The company has only one reportable business segment in which it operates i.e. paper and paperboard including newsprint.  n  n8. Comparative figures of the previous period have been  regrouped/rearranged wherever necessary.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
